IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain

-- g7-interpretation: the fork points of group G7 (Articles 21 to 25, Articles 37 to 43 and the endnotes), as ONE record, one field per fork (the R4 shape of the brief).
-- Each fork point is an enumeration with one constructor per reading; the FIRST constructor is the reading taken, and each field says so with TYPICALLY.
-- Every public decision of G7 that depends on a fork takes this record as an ordinary GIVEN and delegates by CONSIDER to one private implementation per reading.
-- The readings taken are assumed, not ruled: FRAGMENT-G7.md section 2 registers each fork with the text that licenses each reading and the case that tells them apart.
-- A record is built whole (there is no record update in L4), so this module also names the reading taken at every fork and, for each fork, the one record that differs from it
-- at that fork alone, so that a test can call the other reading.  F7.8 is typed with domain.l4's `Unit of a term of imprisonment` (IP35), shared by the groups that carry a term of imprisonment.

-- F7.1: R&O.10/2024 brings the text of 27 February 2024 into force at 9.30 a.m. that day (endnote E9).
DECLARE `Treatment of a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time` IS ONE OF
    `a question about that day alone is refused`
    `the whole day is in the new text`

-- F7.2: R&O.28/2023 Article 3, R&O.56/2025 Article 2, R&O.102/2026 Article 7(6).
DECLARE `Counting of “7 days after it is made”` IS ONE OF
    `the day of making is left out`
    `seven clear days are left`

-- F7.3: endnote Table of Legislation History row L.41/2014 against the Table of Renumbered Provisions.
DECLARE `Numbering that the commencement table speaks in` IS ONE OF
    `the table is in the original numbers`
    `the table is in the present numbers`

-- F7.4: Articles 21(1) with 21(2), 21(3) with 21(4), 21(5) with 21(6), 23(1) with 23(2), and 21(7), 23(5).
DECLARE `How the strict and the knowing offences of Articles 21 and 23 combine for one act` IS ONE OF
    `both offences are made out`
    `the knowing offence displaces the strict one`

-- F7.5: Articles 21(2)(b)(ii) against 21(4)(b)(ii), 21(6)(b)(ii) and 23(2)(b)(ii).
DECLARE `Wording of the advantage limb of the knowing offences` IS ONE OF
    `the wording differs as printed`
    `the wording is harmonised`

-- F7.6: Article 37(1) against Article 2(1)(a) and (i).
DECLARE `Bodies within Article 37(1)` IS ONE OF
    `only partnerships and bodies corporate`
    `also unincorporated associations and trustees`

-- F7.7: Article 38 gives only a power to make an Order about service.
DECLARE `Reading of the date on which a notice is served` IS ONE OF
    `the date of receipt`
    `the date of sending`

-- F7.9: Part 8 (Article 32 against Articles 33 to 36) and Part 9 (Article 37 against Articles 38 to 43).
DECLARE `Treatment of a Part brought into force in two stages` IS ONE OF
    `in force when all its Articles are`
    `in force when any of its Articles is`

-- F7.10: Article 37(1)(a) and (b).
DECLARE `Pairing of a capacity with the kind of body in Article 37(1)` IS ONE OF
    `capacity as printed for each kind of body`
    `any listed capacity for any body`

-- F7.11: every date of the Table of Legislation History; R&O.17/2018 Article 1 and Article 2.
DECLARE `Counting of the day named as the day of commencement` IS ONE OF
    `the named day is the first day in force`
    `the day after the named day is the first day in force`

-- F7.12: Article 22(1) (“For the purpose of Article 21”) against Article 2(10)(b) (“an excepted foreign charity (within the meaning of Article 22)”).
DECLARE `Reach of the definition of an excepted foreign charity in Article 22` IS ONE OF
    `Article 22 defines the term wherever the Law uses it`
    `Article 22 defines the term for Article 21 only`

-- F7.13: Article 24(3)(a) (“may make the provision by adapting any provisions of Articles 21 to 23”) against Article 24(4) (“a penalty no greater than a fine”).
DECLARE `Reach of the cap of Article 24(4) on a penalty adapted from Articles 21 to 23` IS ONE OF
    `the cap of Article 24(4) applies to every offence of the Regulations`
    `the cap of Article 24(4) does not apply to an offence adapted from Articles 21 to 23`

-- F7.14: Article 2(2) (the Minister may by Order add sub-paragraphs to Article 2(1)) against Article 39(1) (“other than an amendment of this Law”) and Article 39(2) (“by Regulations”).
DECLARE `Consequential amendments of this Law by an Order under Article 2(2)` IS ONE OF
    `only Regulations can make consequential amendments of this Law`
    `an Order under Article 2(2) can make them too`

-- The one record of this group's fork points: one field per fork, each TYPICALLY the reading taken (the first constructor of each enumeration).
DECLARE `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
    HAS `how a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time is treated` IS A `Treatment of a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time` TYPICALLY `a question about that day alone is refused`
        `how “7 days after it is made” is counted` IS A `Counting of “7 days after it is made”` TYPICALLY `the day of making is left out`
        `the numbering the commencement table speaks in` IS A `Numbering that the commencement table speaks in` TYPICALLY `the table is in the original numbers`
        `how the strict and the knowing offences combine for one act` IS A `How the strict and the knowing offences of Articles 21 and 23 combine for one act` TYPICALLY `both offences are made out`
        `the wording of the advantage limb of the knowing offences` IS A `Wording of the advantage limb of the knowing offences` TYPICALLY `the wording differs as printed`
        `the bodies within Article 37(1)` IS A `Bodies within Article 37(1)` TYPICALLY `only partnerships and bodies corporate`
        `the date on which a notice is served` IS A `Reading of the date on which a notice is served` TYPICALLY `the date of receipt`
        `the unit of a term of imprisonment` IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` TYPICALLY `calendar months`
        `how a Part brought into force in two stages is treated` IS A `Treatment of a Part brought into force in two stages` TYPICALLY `in force when all its Articles are`
        `how capacity is paired with the kind of body in Article 37(1)` IS A `Pairing of a capacity with the kind of body in Article 37(1)` TYPICALLY `capacity as printed for each kind of body`
        `how the day named as the day of commencement is counted` IS A `Counting of the day named as the day of commencement` TYPICALLY `the named day is the first day in force`
        `whether Article 22 defines an excepted foreign charity outside Article 21` IS A `Reach of the definition of an excepted foreign charity in Article 22` TYPICALLY `Article 22 defines the term wherever the Law uses it`
        `whether adapting Articles 21 to 23 under Article 24(3)(a) can carry their imprisonment` IS A `Reach of the cap of Article 24(4) on a penalty adapted from Articles 21 to 23` TYPICALLY `the cap of Article 24(4) applies to every offence of the Regulations`
        `whether an Order under Article 2(2) can make consequential amendments of other provisions of the Law` IS A `Consequential amendments of this Law by an Order under Article 2(2)` TYPICALLY `only Regulations can make consequential amendments of this Law`

-- The reading taken at every fork (assumed, not ruled).
`the favoured interpretation` MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` WITH
        `how a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time is treated` IS `a question about that day alone is refused`
        `how “7 days after it is made” is counted` IS `the day of making is left out`
        `the numbering the commencement table speaks in` IS `the table is in the original numbers`
        `how the strict and the knowing offences combine for one act` IS `both offences are made out`
        `the wording of the advantage limb of the knowing offences` IS `the wording differs as printed`
        `the bodies within Article 37(1)` IS `only partnerships and bodies corporate`
        `the date on which a notice is served` IS `the date of receipt`
        `the unit of a term of imprisonment` IS `calendar months`
        `how a Part brought into force in two stages is treated` IS `in force when all its Articles are`
        `how capacity is paired with the kind of body in Article 37(1)` IS `capacity as printed for each kind of body`
        `how the day named as the day of commencement is counted` IS `the named day is the first day in force`
        `whether Article 22 defines an excepted foreign charity outside Article 21` IS `Article 22 defines the term wherever the Law uses it`
        `whether adapting Articles 21 to 23 under Article 24(3)(a) can carry their imprisonment` IS `the cap of Article 24(4) applies to every offence of the Regulations`
        `whether an Order under Article 2(2) can make consequential amendments of other provisions of the Law` IS `only Regulations can make consequential amendments of this Law`

-- IP35: the unit of a term of imprisonment is shared by four groups (G6 F6.16, G7 F7.8, G8 F8.8, G9 F9.13); the integrator sets it from one value.  This builds the record with that unit and every other fork as taken.
GIVEN unit IS A `Unit of a term of imprisonment` @desc The unit in which a term of imprisonment is measured
GIVETH AN `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
`the favoured interpretation with the unit of a term of imprisonment` unit MEANS
    `Interpretation of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes` WITH
        `how a day on which a text takes effect at a stated time is treated` IS `a question about that day alone is refused`
        `how “7 days after it is made” is counted` IS `the day of making is left out`
        `the numbering the commencement table speaks in` IS `the table is in the original numbers`
        `how the strict and the knowing offences combine for one act` IS `both offences are made out`
        `the wording of the advantage limb of the knowing offences` IS `the wording differs as printed`
        `the bodies within Article 37(1)` IS `only partnerships and bodies corporate`
        `the date on which a notice is served` IS `the date of receipt`
        `the unit of a term of imprisonment` IS unit
        `how a Part brought into force in two stages is treated` IS `in force when all its Articles are`
        `how capacity is paired with the kind of body in Article 37(1)` IS `capacity as printed for each kind of body`
        `how the day named as the day of commencement is counted` IS `the named day is the first day in force`
        `whether Article 22 defines an excepted foreign charity outside Article 21` IS `Article 22 defines the term wherever the Law uses it`
        `whether adapting Articles 21 to 23 under Article 24(3)(a) can carry their imprisonment` IS `the cap of Article 24(4) applies to every offence of the Regulations`
        `whether an Order under Article 2(2) can make consequential amendments of other provisions of the Law` IS `only Regulations can make consequential amendments of this Law`

